From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:22:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: Stop CE receive refill before teardown

The CE refill timer can still touch receive rings after the driver
stops CE interrupts. Stop the timer before error unwinds release the
rings and before PCI power down. Share the IRQ and timer stop sequence
with the PCI stop callback.

Codex consolidated the two fixes and compared the resulting kernel tree.
The Piano suspend and recovery tests covered PCI CE stop and refill.

Fixes: d889913205cf ("wifi: ath12k: driver for Qualcomm Wi-Fi 7 devices")
Link: https://docs.kernel.org/driver-api/basics.html#c.timer_delete_sync
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c  |  1 +
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c |  1 +
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c  | 10 +++++++++-
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
index 9549be24e..23a6f4db3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
@@ -1241,6 +1241,7 @@ static int ath12k_ahb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	return 0;
 
 err_deinit_arch:
+	timer_shutdown_sync(&ab->rx_replenish_retry);
 	ab_ahb->device_family_ops->arch_deinit(ab);
 
 err_rproc_deconfigure:
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
index ab2ea9932..64edcd2de 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -2262,6 +2262,7 @@ err_unassign_hw_group:
 
 void ath12k_core_deinit(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
+	timer_shutdown_sync(&ab->rx_replenish_retry);
 	ath12k_core_hw_group_destroy(ab->ag);
 	ath12k_core_hw_group_unassign(ab);
 }
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
index 67a1b9b8e..39ed65523 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
@@ -987,6 +987,12 @@ static void ath12k_pci_ce_irq_disable_sync(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 	ath12k_pci_cancel_workqueue(ab);
 }
 
+static void ath12k_pci_ce_stop(struct ath12k_base *ab)
+{
+	ath12k_pci_ce_irq_disable_sync(ab);
+	timer_delete_sync(&ab->rx_replenish_retry);
+}
+
 int ath12k_pci_map_service_to_pipe(struct ath12k_base *ab, u16 service_id,
 				   u8 *ul_pipe, u8 *dl_pipe)
 {
@@ -1161,7 +1167,7 @@ void ath12k_pci_stop(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 	if (!test_bit(ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_INIT_DONE, &ab_pci->flags))
 		return;
 
-	ath12k_pci_ce_irq_disable_sync(ab);
+	ath12k_pci_ce_stop(ab);
 	ath12k_ce_cleanup_pipes(ab);
 }
 
@@ -1494,6 +1500,8 @@ void ath12k_pci_power_down(struct ath12k_base *ab, bool is_suspend)
 	if (!test_bit(ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_INIT_DONE, &ab_pci->flags))
 		return;
 
+	ath12k_pci_ce_stop(ab);
+
 	/* restore aspm in case firmware bootup fails */
 	ath12k_pci_aspm_restore(ab_pci);
 
-- 
